    "text": "VERDICT: NOT SUPPORTED. Time in market 76.0%. (a) Mean top-layer forget-gate correlates r=-0.58 with Close/SMA200-1 and r=-0.32 with the 20-day SMA_200 slope (pooled Pearson); median per-fold |r| of cell-state PC1 = 0.76 / 0.39 (placebo 50-day trend: 0.75; a 200-day-specific memory should beat the placebo) -> met (needs pooled |r|>=0.3 and PC1 |r|>=0.5). (b) in 6 scored OOS crash window(s) the strategy had a shallower MDD than an exposure-matched constant-weight Buy & Hold in 2; mean return -28.12% vs Buy & Hold -32.25%; flat 31.16% of crash days vs 24.00% overall (needs >=10 pp more flat in crashes) -> not met. (c) Removing the 200-day features at test time changes directional accuracy by up to -0.56 pp and MDD by up to 1.88 pp (baseline DA 49.63%, MDD -70.53%) -> not met (needs DA drop >=1 pp or MDD worsening >=2 pp). SKILL CHECK: corr(predicted, actual next-day return) = -0.027; up-day base rate 50.6% (directional accuracy 49.63% is only meaningful relative to it); average daily return when long 4.9 bps vs flat 10.3 bps. TIMING CHECK: strategy Sharpe 0.39 / MDD -70.53% vs a constant 76% Buy & Hold Sharpe 0.57 / MDD -50.15% - lower drawdown than full Buy & Hold is only evidence of skill if it beats this. CAVEATS: the initial training window runs to 2011-03-24 and contains the whole 2008 crash, so no 2008 claim is out-of-sample; the LSTM has 54,081 parameters vs 13,569 for a same-size Simple RNN (capacity confound); trade thresholds are tuned on validation data that also drives early stopping (mild optimism); gate/cell-state correlations between smooth trending series can be spurious and units are not comparable across retrained folds. WARNING: median best epoch is 1 - the networks stop almost immediately, so gate values stay near their initialisation and (a) says little about learned memory. Heuristic thresholds; 1/3 criteria met."
